{
  "requirement": "When `habeas author` assesses a subject with existing evidence, that evidence\nMUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment. Its inputs,\ndetermination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` or otherwise be\nsupplied to the model. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs\nsupplied to it, so sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer\nexist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.**\n\n**Implementation**\n\n- **Existing evidence only decides whether to assess.**\n  - `author_all_with_options` (src/authoring/batch.rs) loads existing evidence with `LoadedDetailEvidence::load` and uses only its `state()` to decide whether to skip a subject. Valid, FIXME and still-current false judgments are skipped. Missing and Invalid evidence is reassessed.\n  - Nothing from the old record is passed on. The batch hands only the subject name to `prepare_assessment`, and `configured_record` then calls `AssessmentSources::prepare(root, name)`.\n- **No contribution to the mandatory input set.**\n  - `AssessmentSources::prepare` (src/authoring/inputs.rs) builds the mandatory set from the subject, its `{cite}` targets, the subject's `{impl}`/`{test}` references and anchors, and term definitions. It never opens `evidence/<name>.json`.\n  - Selectors that fall under generated `evidence/` are omitted. This goes through `omit_generated_evidence` (src/authoring/access.rs), `generated_evidence_path` and `generated_evidence_selector`, and it covers symlink aliases and honors workspace allow/disallow policy.\n  - The model sees only `sources.mandatory_inputs()` through `initial_prompt` and the tool results. Because old inputs are never read, ones that no longer exist cannot block reassessment.\n- **New evidence records only inputs supplied.**\n  - `recorded` starts empty in `prepare`.\n  - In `assess` (src/authoring/mod.rs), `record_inputs(&pending)` runs only after a provider response is accepted. `pending` is the mandatory set plus tool deliveries.\n  - The evidence JSON uses `sources.recorded_inputs()`, so nothing carries over from an earlier record.\n- The `{impl}` markings are complete for the behavior involved. The behavior beyond this requirement (generated-evidence omission) is covered by `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` and `requirements.configuration.evidence_paths`, which the same code marks as implemented.\n\n**Tests** (src/authoring/inputs.rs, all marked `{test}` for this requirement)\n\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` writes old evidence with `determination: false`, a rationale and a `notes.txt` input. It asserts that the mandatory set does not contain `notes.txt` or the old rationale, that `recorded_inputs()` is empty, and that the digest and `{impl}`/`{test}` edges are right.\n- `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` puts a missing file, a removed Rust item and a removed requirement in the old record. `prepare` still succeeds and yields exactly the subject input.\n- `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` includes an old input that points at the evidence file itself. It asserts that nothing from the old record is supplied and that the old file is left untouched.\n- Other tests, such as `generated_evidence_is_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery` in src/authoring/tools.rs, cover generated-evidence exclusion, including symlink aliases.\n\n**Minor limitation.** No test runs the full `assess` or batch path with prior evidence on disk and then checks the final record's `inputs`. That property follows structurally from `recorded` starting empty and being filled only from delivered inputs. Tests in src/authoring/mod.rs check that the final record matches what was delivered (for example `record[\"inputs\"] == mandatory_inputs`). I treat this as adequate coverage, not a gap.",
  "references": "58dcaf6317c3e8d5596c53062b30ed6564a1f357f54b3d3b68f21305c9506694",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.authoring_inputs",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.authoring_inputs"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} authoring_inputs",
        "When `habeas author` assesses a subject with existing evidence, that evidence",
        "MUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment. Its inputs,",
        "determination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set",
        "defined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` or otherwise be",
        "supplied to the model. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs",
        "supplied to it, so sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer",
        "exist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} mandatory_inputs",
        "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining",
        "the contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and",
        "its inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and",
        "define which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every",
        "applicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report",
        "unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied",
        "in the initial model request.",
        "Generated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST",
        "be omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit",
        "workspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort",
        "under {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
